    "narrative": "Ghost Ride the WHIP enters today\u2019s slate prioritizing high-ceiling volume against soft-tossing righties. **Corbin Carroll** leads the squad with a 71.36 score, buoyed by a favorable hitting environment and a prime #2 spot against Nola. His ability to impact the SB category remains the core driver for his high-end projection. **Brice Turang** (64.21) also warrants attention; despite facing a team with an elite hold rate, his lead-off position provides enough stolen base upside to mitigate the pitcher\u2019s competency. Similarly, **Mickey Moniak** (62.71) benefits from a massive 14% park boost, allowing him to capitalize on the matchup against Povich despite the platoon disadvantage. **Austin Riley** (63.42) remains a start-worthy anchor, as his 19% SP skill edge against Molina compensates for a lower spot in the order, ensuring he remains a focal point for power production.\n\nThe optimization process for today was tight, specifically regarding the benching of **Cole Young** (40.21) and **Max Muncy** (40.17). While both offered moderate utility, they were ultimately sidelined because their projected efficiency was squeezed by the superior situational matchups assigned to **Zach McKinstry** and **Edwin Arroyo**. We are monitoring the status of **James Wood** and **Vinnie Pasquantino**, who remain out of contention today, leaving us with a thinner bench than ideal for covering potential late-game lineup pivots. Caution is advised regarding **Gabriel Moreno** and **Josh Naylor**; both are facing tougher than average arms, and with **Gabriel Moreno** slotted into the #3 hole, any early defensive replacements could prematurely cap our production for the day. Managers should keep a close eye on the weather and potential late-scratches, as our reliance on **Zach McKinstry**\u2019s specific utility profile leaves little room for error if his status changes.",
